{"event_type":"review","id":"0342d1db5d3a59bedfe29a9db2047db328532ff0f9722b9192ac8c26a1a07215","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T13:59:23Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/aec29b19cc640f4941a0fb10763b7f22dac8d0458fd039e60d38c72dc0383fa3","sha256":"aec29b19cc640f4941a0fb10763b7f22dac8d0458fd039e60d38c72dc0383fa3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a03ccdd8c3bf10c3429e24868c98e6671a4a3b9d0ba91be16427af0cda1766e5","sha256":"a03ccdd8c3bf10c3429e24868c98e6671a4a3b9d0ba91be16427af0cda1766e5"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/90d86fd28d8f4eac32cc06ca2aa978339e77b250156b6b54a33912dfbad1a8be","sha256":"90d86fd28d8f4eac32cc06ca2aa978339e77b250156b6b54a33912dfbad1a8be"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e89584e7626e6ac3147398c6f1baf6baacd59a646c8fed90724831d7129b15c1","sha256":"e89584e7626e6ac3147398c6f1baf6baacd59a646c8fed90724831d7129b15c1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/edc6fd72ac269c8f08f461626fb5354a0e16f313deaa23a4c51948b7aaa96a0d","sha256":"edc6fd72ac269c8f08f461626fb5354a0e16f313deaa23a4c51948b7aaa96a0d"}],"attempt_id":"3e5f3975f0d75c34bc0f004476f1f69fb90a37d8ee373409ce04674bf281fcdf:0:1","base":"a0623ffeaaecca07d4e1748c5e2a7e9ee5e1b49e","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"781df27181b6cb3da3772889cc49c374c6bbd127","body":"**`FixableReviewItemSchema.comments` rejects the `authorType` field that `ThreadComment` allows.**\n\n`ThreadComment` (src/ops/review/threads.ts:14-23) declares an optional `authorType`. The inline comment object at Lines 462-466 is `.strict()` and omits that key. Any `review.fixItem` item whose prior comment carries `authorType` fails validation at the JSON boundary. This contradicts the doc comment at Lines 440-452, which says the mirror must accept what the fetch produces. `ThreadCommentSchema` at Line 105 already accepts `authorType`.\n\nReuse `ThreadCommentSchema` instead of the inline object.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     comments: z\n-      .array(\n-        z\n-          .object({\n-            authorLogin: z.string().nullable(),\n-            body: z.string(),\n-            createdAt: z.string().min(1).nullable(),\n-          })\n-          .strict(),\n-      )\n+      .array(ThreadCommentSchema)\n       .max(100),\n```\n</details>","id":"a59e18c7c83692bf73aad5835b8d47582ca08eb38b7311d11afd6c15b78c0ece","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/registry.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`FixableReviewItemSchema.comments` rejects the `authorType` field that `ThreadComment` allows."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"fe12026c0aefce265530ca4848788d07f757e262","body":"**The readiness section reaches the tracker PR body without a denylist scan.**\n\n`src/ops/pr/assemblePrs.ts:282-287` refuses any publication when no `DiffSecretScanner` is configured. It also scans every body right before `editPrBody` (`assemblePrs.ts:412`). `makeRunReport` writes to the same tracker body but takes no scanner and never calls one.\n\nThis section contains text that nobody has checked. `reason` holds raw `gh` fault text (`readiness: ${snapshot.message}` at Line 141), which comes from `gh`'s stderr. `name` is a value supplied by the caller. `mdSafe` and `singleLine` only clean up markdown and control characters. They do not detect secrets. Content that the assembler would refuse can therefore reach the forge through this second writer.\n\nFix: take a `publicationScanner` the same way `makeAssemblePrs` does. Return `failed` when no scanner is given. Scan the composed body inside the lock before `editPrBody`. One way to share the logic is to export `scanPublicationForUpload` from `assemblePrs.ts`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n           const current = await gh.getPrBody(trackerNumber);\n-          await gh.editPrBody(\n-            trackerNumber,\n-            composeSection(current, reportSection(input.runPrefix, rows)),\n-          );\n+          const body = composeSection(current, reportSection(input.runPrefix, rows));\n+          await scanPublicationForUpload(publicationScanner, undefined, body);\n+          await gh.editPrBody(trackerNumber, body);\n```\n\nAlso add `publicationScanner?: DiffSecretScanner` to `makeRunReport`. When `input.tracker !== undefined` and the scanner is missing, return `failed`. Update the registry importer so it passes the scanner in.\n</details>","id":"88c05b70072323b2cf6817a7647848cc300e2a85db2d2e9f95caeafbd0b2b809","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/pr/runReport.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The readiness section reaches the tracker PR body without a denylist scan."}],"head":"d6d68a24f1b769529fc0b8ee684923229142ce56","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"2587ab2579715ec180cb061f29947ac9841cfb44","intervals":[[1,416]],"path":"src/ops/ledger/ledger.ts"},{"blob":"c48b386ed96d6690625dd315d6ddcfa615d710c1","intervals":[[1,867]],"path":"src/ops/pr/assemblePrs.ts"},{"blob":"baef0f61c6d6120ec3feb900740d2e6ed96e4486","intervals":[[1,318]],"path":"src/ops/pr/ensureTrackerBranch.ts"},{"blob":"fe12026c0aefce265530ca4848788d07f757e262","intervals":[[1,509]],"path":"src/ops/pr/runReport.ts"},{"blob":"0fb113490d1cb4ade21b057d2b7237c9dcc1d834","intervals":[[1,114]],"path":"src/ops/ratchet/recomputeTypecheck.ts"},{"blob":"baaf5255f1c093bea7dec2b895305884071a21cf","intervals":[[1,873]],"path":"src/ops/review/fixReviewItem.ts"},{"blob":"781df27181b6cb3da3772889cc49c374c6bbd127","intervals":[[1,783]],"path":"src/ops/review/registry.ts"},{"blob":"c83d4f6ac66b900fc5a2ec3643a3a7ecffd8817d","intervals":[[1,897]],"path":"src/ops/sweep/planSweep.ts"}],"job_id":"3e5f3975f0d75c34bc0f00